-- title:
--   Flatness of X→ X₁ and primes of the level stalk
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field, $A\subseteq L$ a valuation subring such that for all $a,b\in A$ with $a$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $b\neq 0$ there is $n\in\mathbb N$ with $b\mid a^{n}$. Let $X$ be an integral scheme with a proper, flat, locally of finite presentation morphism $\mathrm{toBase}:X\to\operatorname{Spec}A$. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain, $\iota_0:A_0\to A$ an injective local ring homomorphism, $\varpi_0$ a generator of the maximal ideal of $A_0$, and suppose every element of $A$ is algebraic over the image subring $\iota_0(A_0)$. Let $X_0$ be integral with $\mathrm{toBase}_0:X_0\to\operatorname{Spec}A_0$ proper, flat and locally of finite presentation, together with an isomorphism $X\cong X_0\times_{\operatorname{Spec}A_0}\operatorname{Spec}A$ whose composite with the second projection is $\mathrm{toBase}$. Let $x\in X$ lie over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}A$ and admit no proper specialisation (every $y$ with $x\rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$), and let $x_0\in X_0$ be its image under the isomorphism followed by the first projection. Let $w\ge 1$ and let $e$ be a ring isomorphism from the completion of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X_0,x_0}$ at its maximal ideal onto $\widehat A_0[[u,v]]/(uv-\varpi_0^{w})$, where $\widehat A_0$ is the completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal and the quotient is of the power series ring in two variables by the ideal generated by $u v-C(\varpi_0^{w})$; assume $e$ carries the image in the completion of the germ at $x_0$ of the global section of $X_0$ pulled back from $a\in A_0$ to the class of the constant series $C(a)$. Finally let $A_1$ be a discrete valuation domain, $\iota_1':A_0\to A_1$ and $\iota_1:A_1\to A$ local homomorphisms with $\iota_1$ injective and $\iota_1\circ\iota_1'=\iota_0$, let $\varpi_1$ generate the maximal ideal of $A_1$, let $g_1:X_1\to X_0$ and $f_1:X_1\to\operatorname{Spec}A_1$ form a pullback square over $\mathrm{toBase}_0$ and $\operatorname{Spec}\iota_1'$, and let $e_1:X\cong X_1\times_{\operatorname{Spec}A_1}\operatorname{Spec}A$ be an isomorphism whose composite with the second projection is $\mathrm{toBase}$ and whose composite with the first projection followed by $g_1$ agrees with the isomorphism to $X_0$-side first projection. Write $\pi:X\to X_1$ for $e_1$ followed by the first projection. Then $g_1(\pi(x))=x_0$; $\pi$ is flat; and for every prime ideal $\mathfrak q$ of $\mathcal O_{X_1,\pi(x)}$ other than its maximal ideal there are $y\in X$ with $y\rightsquigarrow x$ and $y\neq x$ such that $\mathfrak q$ is the preimage of the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{X,y}$ under $\mathcal O_{X_1,\pi(x)}\to\mathcal O_{X,x}\to\mathcal O_{X,y}$, the first map being the stalk map of $\pi$ at $x$ and the second the specialisation map.
--
--   This is a step in the analysis of a semistable (crossing) point of a proper flat integral model after descending the base to a discrete valuation ring and interposing an intermediate discrete valuation level $A_1$: it identifies the image of the special point in $X_0$, establishes flatness of the projection to the level model, and describes all non-maximal primes of the level stalk as contractions of maximal ideals at proper generisations of $x$. It is used in the proof that the stalk of the base-changed model is integrally closed ([`AlgebraicGeometry.isIntegrallyClosed_stalk_pullback_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_of_isDiscreteValuationRing`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.isIntegrallyClosed_stalk_pullback_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_of_isDiscreteValuationRing)).
